WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.640
The Mother of Dragons has opened up about
some of her biggest behind-the-scenes battles.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.200
In the months after the extraordinarily divisive
ending of Game of Thrones, which closed out

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:14.610
its epic eight-season run in May 2019, Emilia
Clarke, who played Daenerys Targaryen on the

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:19.000
series, has spoken out about tough moments
she experienced during filming, namely the

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.300
scenes in which she appeared in the buff,
and there were quite a few.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.400
Speaking with actor Dax Shepard on his podcast
Armchair Expert, Clarke got candid about the

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:32.079
pressure to perform while baring it all and
the toll it took on her, especially considering

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.640
the fact that she was quite young when she
began her tenure on Thrones.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.620
Clarke told Shepard that she suffered from
serious imposter syndrome while filming, saying,

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.080
"I'd been on a film set twice before then,
and now I'm on a film set completely naked,

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.190
with all of these people and I don't know
what I'm meant to do, and I don't know what's

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:51.300
expected of me, and I don't know what you
want, and I don't know what I want."

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.780
She told Shepard that both her clothed and
unclothed scenes on Game of Thrones caused

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.240
her feelings of anxiety and self-doubt.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.480
Luckily, Clarke had an ally in Aquaman himself,
Jason Momoa, who played her husband Khal Drogo

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.140
during the show's first season.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:08.660
Momoa completely had her back during these
difficult sequences.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.040
"He was an experienced actor who had done
a bunch of stuff before coming on to this,

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.760
he was like, 'Sweetie, this is how it's meant
to be and this is how it's not meant to be,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.560
and I'm going to make sure that's the way
it f---ing goes.'"

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.020
Clearly, Momoa was warmly protective of Clarke,
who appreciated it immensely.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.200
"He was so kind.."

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:25.840
"He's a prince."

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.500
"That's great."

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.000
"Yeah.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.200
And considerate and cared about me as a human
being."

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.100
However, as more time went by, Clarke realized
she had the clout to stick up for herself

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.360
on set, saying that she became "a lot more
savvy" about what she's comfortable doing.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:44.780
"Like, I've had fights on set before where
I'm like, 'No, the sheet stays up.'

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.880
And they're like, 'You don't want to disappoint
your Game of Thrones fans,' and I'm like,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.040
'F--- you.'"

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:54.020
By the time she had to perform her final nude
scene, which took place on the season 6 episode

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.620
"Book of the Stranger," Clarke took control,
saying,

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.580
"I'm owning this, this is mine, they've asked
me to do it, and I am f---ing game."

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.280
Game of Thrones featured plenty of full-frontal
scenes during its decade-long run, and Clarke

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.560
performed her fair share.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.220
From her wedding night with Khal Drogo to
her rebirth from the flames that gave way

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:14.760
to her dragons, some of those sequences actually
made sense within the plot of the show.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.599
Beyond that, there were a handful of scenes
during which Clarke's Daenerys simply stripped

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.580
down for no narrative reason, which obviously
took its toll on the actress.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:27.680
Thrones became infamous throughout its run
for using sex and nudity as narrative devices

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:31.939
even when it barely made sense to do so, and
clearly, the comments made to Clarke about

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.320
keeping her fans "happy" was no outlier.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.960
Director Neil Marshall, who helmed the season
2 episode "Blackwater," once opened up about

00:02:38.969 --> 00:02:44.280
how studio executives pushed him to add titillation
when it wasn't needed, proving that HBO brass

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.370
were likely more concerned with ratings than
how the Game of Thrones cast and crew felt

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.900
about the on-set environment.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.640
In the end, it's great that Clarke found the
strength to stand up for herself and that

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.239
stars like Momoa stuck up for her when she
couldn't, but it's unsettling that the higher-ups

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.660
behind Game of Thrones pushed such a young
actress into performing scenes that made her

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.500
uncomfortable.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.160
Ultimately, Clarke is clearly still proud
of the show that brought her international

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:11.749
fame, and how she handled this important on-set
dilemma will almost definitely help young

00:03:11.749 --> 00:03:13.180
stars going forward.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:19.040
If you miss Khaleesi, Game of Thrones is streaming
in its entirety on HBO Go and HBO On Demand.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.080
If you want to catch Clarke in a new role,
her latest film, Last Christmas, is in theaters

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:23.880
now.

